hash":"87f88a5649ef657abc745949425d27e3f0c450f1ae0af53a6a8a036933da7a09","event_uuid":"d17d9ea4-b5fb-4850-b87d-b78ab072c7db","position":{"commit_sha":"c5f79ce3c9ec3345f3426dab42a65d16483b068e","position":"1795114068522782581-d17d9ea4-b5fb-4850-b87d-b78ab072c7db"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"20336a664e4114eeddd9028039d302e9e1500c6f242782a5051fc98fd4350728","event_uuid":"685b5326-53a1-4dc7-8b7f-32d62f4b43df","position":{"commit_sha":"e7f2c0ec05def8d09b11d28d9bb1e3918e247117","position":"1795114074912299535-685b5326-53a1-4dc7-8b7f-32d62f4b43df"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ca2b17593643e8622e5a0e6ac82810b09112329bacbbf69d9617973e395b7cda","event_uuid":"43235c26-1954-4633-b26c-3e5462c15833","position":{"commit_sha":"10da18be543cf9544ce24a0ae255adec812304ae","position":"1795115383330275805-43235c26-1954-4633-b26c-3e5462c15833"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b2e74fc319213ca2d1f285949ee4a9486b238adb8ccf1703d95595333db37415","event_uuid":"31e14ae6-c54a-4147-9c98-2b376b8d3b4a","position":{"commit_sha":"4b3685f16d6e0840d22d429198940f077f57ba1b","position":"1795117084188521612-31e14ae6-c54a-4147-9c98-2b376b8d3b4a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"3b19291efd6bf635787ea0f66c595efecc4ab7a520b1fcc16a2ae6ad5c6a6b8f","event_uuid":"d4da0e66-5d57-4f45-9f91-a31dcdb9a2f3","position":{"commit_sha":"7b50a592cfef665a265f8e3e41b55157c7303070","position":"1795117544692371964-d4da0e66-5d57-4f45-9f91-a31dcdb9a2f3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"09b1e6c7d6c481c5892041a82a9b07892993c7fbec6fe890fd070c15d46ab325","event_uuid":"21a9b429-e474-4b0e-9f38-05688c8a5f00","position":{"commit_sha":"7b50a592cfef665a265f8e3e41b55157c7303070","position":"1795117544707624732-21a9b429-e474-4b0e-9f38-05688c8a5f00"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795112489769239285,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nADR 0049 (`docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md`) pins trusted op-cert environment keys in the repository file `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, and ADR 0104 (`docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md`, decision 3 and its env_id note) builds the MCP server's enforcement plan on that pin file. The operator decided on 2026-11-19 (epic nonblack-brigandish-guillemot) that op-cert keys must not be hardcoded in the repository. This task records that decision as a new ADR before any code changes, so the later stories implement a written decision.\n\n## Approach\nWrite `docs/adr/0125-opcert-trust-per-environment.md` and reserve the number with the marker file `docs/adr/.numbers/0125` (content `0125-opcert-trust-per-environment.md`, as `docs/adr/.numbers/0124` holds its slug); `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` (run by `make lint`) requires it, and its add/add conflict blocks a duplicate claim at merge. Regenerate `docs/adr/README.md` with `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` rather than hand-editing it. Header: `Status: Accepted`, `Date: 2026-11-19`, `Ticket: calcite-cursed-lovebird / 02a7-a3ed-f72e-42b1`, `Epic: nonblack-brigandish-guillemot / 0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90` (the ADR 0124 shape); sections Context, Decision, Consequences, Alternatives rejected. Context describes today's trust root (own key, then pinned key, then embedded key; bug c21f) and its problems. The Decision records:\n1. Principle: identity, authorization and op-cert certification are separate. Anyone can sign a plan review, code review or completion verification; signing is never gated on an allowed identity or key.\n2. Default verification is validity-only: the SSHSIG signature verifies under the key embedded in it, for the certificate's principal and the `rebar.opcert.v1` namespace, and the signed subject binds ticket, kind and material. The result reports `signing_key` (a `SHA256:` fingerprint) and the environment (principal). Trust bases after the change: `envelope_key` (validity-only) and `trust_list`; `own_key` and `pinned_environment` are removed.\n3. Optional per-environment trust list `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` (env override `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS`), entries `<env_id> <key-type> <base64> [comment]`, held in the verifying environment's own configuration (user config, env var, deployment, or a CI job's protected variables); the repository's `rebar.toml` does not set it. Listed (principal, key) passes with `trust_list`; a valid but unlisted pair is `untrusted`; a malformed list fails closed. No eras: rotation keeps retired keys listed while their certificates matter; on compromise the key is removed, which untrusts all its certificates.\n4. `verify.require_environment` keeps its meaning and now requires a trust list (a principal is a self-claim); without one it refuses with `foreign_key`. The merge gate `rebar verify-opcert` uses the gating environment's list; enabling enforcement means setting require_environment, opcert_enforce_since and the list in that environment.\n5. `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `rebar trusted-env`, and the pin file's log-position key eras are removed; signing never consults a list.\n6. Rebar's MCP server is configured through its deployment (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`, `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`) with the 3 keys the operator listed: its own environment 9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65 (current and rotated `nava-opcert-prod` keys) and environment ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5 (`rebar-opcert`), which the operator chose to keep trusted. This lands before the code stops reading the pin file.\nConsequences: developer clones, CI and review-bot become validity-only; certificates from unlisted environments read `untrusted` on the MCP server; vocabulary changes (`untrusted`, `trust_list`, `signing_key`); rotation is a config change. Rejected alternatives: keep the repo pin file; per-key eras in the list; gating signing on a pinned key.\nSet ADR 0049's status line to `Accepted; repository key pinning superseded by ADR 0125`, and add a note naming ADR 0125 at ADR 0104 decision 3 and at its env_id note.\n\n## Scope\n- `docs/adr/0125-opcert-trust-per-environment.md` (new), `docs/adr/.numbers/0125` (new marker)\n- `docs/adr/README.md` (regenerated by `scripts/gen_adr_index.py`)\n- `docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md` (status line only; body kept as the historical record)\n- `docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md` (notes at decision 3 and its env_id note)\nOut of scope: code, config, deployment and other docs (later stories of the epic).\n\n## Testing\nDocumentation-only; no new testable behavior. `make verify` runs `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` (marker present) through `make lint`. The ADR index drift check, `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check`, runs only in the CI docs-gates action (`.github/actions/docs-gates/action.yml`), so it is run explicitly as an acceptance check. Existing `tests/unit/test_opcert_adr_6a89.py` asserts ADR 0049 still contains `trusted_environments.yaml`, `rebar.opcert.v1` and `ADR 0046`; the body is kept. Portability: Markdown only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0125-opcert-trust-per-environment.md` exists with the header values above and Context, Decision, Consequences and Alternatives sections; its Decision states items 1-6, including `verify.trusted_opcert_keys`, `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS`, the entry format, `untrusted`, `trust_list`, `signing_key`, the no-eras rule, the require_environment rule, and the land-the-list-first ordering (checked by reading the merged file).\n- [ ] `docs/adr/.numbers/0125` exists, `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` exits 0, and `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] `git grep -n 'superseded by ADR 0125' -- docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md` hits the Status line; `git grep -c 'ADR 0125' -- docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md` is at least 2; `git grep -n '0125-opcert-trust-per-environment.md' -- docs/adr/README.md` hits the index entry.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green, and the change lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0125-opcert-trust-per-environment.md","reason":"new ADR"},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0125","reason":"ADR number marker"},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"regenerated index"},{"path":"docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md","reason":"status line: pinning superseded by ADR 0125"},{"path":"docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md","reason":"notes pointing to ADR 0125"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90","parent_status_uuid":"d4da0e66-5d57-4f45-9f91-a31dcdb9a2f3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"02a7-a3ed-f72e-42b1","ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR 0125: op-cert trust is validity-only by default; per-environment trust lists replace repo-pinned keys","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b95a8f5a-3abf-4bb6-9351-66ec11c096b3","c66b41e8-2214-4802-af56-44a727962824","d17d9ea4-b5fb-4850-b87d-b78ab072c7db","685b5326-53a1-4dc7-8b7f-32d62f4b43df","43235c26-1954-4633-b26c-3e5462c15833","31e14ae6-c54a-4147-9c98-2b376b8d3b4a","d4da0e66-5d57-4f45-9f91-a31dcdb9a2f3","21a9b429-e474-4b0e-9f38-05688c8a5f00"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795117544707624733,"uuid":"d7ca5a1c-d082-41e0-83cd-aabd70f12e0a"}